# NOTE: `netlify deploy` does NOT read this file.
#
# It was committed here believing Netlify honoured it. Verified against the live
# site: every path below still returned HTTP 200 after a deploy, because the
# upload is built from the folder contents rather than filtered by this list.
# `ensureNetlifyIgnore` inside the Netlify CLI only appends `.netlify` to
# .gitignore, and is called from link/init/create/dev/serve, never from deploy.
#
# The pattern list is kept as the single source of truth for what must stay
# private. scripts/build-publish.js enforces it by staging public/, and
# scripts/check-publish.js asserts the result. netlify.toml points publish at
# that folder.
#
# Patterns that must never be publicly reachable:
#   firebase/** .firebaserc firebase.json
#   scripts/** tests/** node_modules/** .firebase/**
#   package.json package-lock.json playwright.config.js
#   .git/** .github/** .gitignore .netlifyignore netlify.toml
#   QA_REPORT.md MVP-AUDIT.md DEPLOYMENT_CHECKLIST.md MIGRATION_GUIDE.md
#   README.md *.docx *.log

# Operational note for humans only, not a deploy filter:
# Deploying this site means:
#   npm run publish:prepare
#   netlify deploy --prod --dir public